@startuml acceptance-check
' cumin works - the states of a requirement issue around the acceptance check.
' Document: acceptance-check.md, section on the changed rows of issue-states.md.
' The red arrow and the red guards are the change. Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the agents work on the sub-issues

state "awaiting-plan-review" as PlanReview
PlanReview : do / a Maintainer reviews the plan and the sub-issues

state "accepting" as Accepting
Accepting : do / the Planner checks the merged work\nand creates the fix sub-issues once

state "awaiting-acceptance" as Acceptance
Acceptance : do / a Maintainer decides the acceptance

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / a Maintainer answers

Implementing --> Accepting : request the acceptance check\n[every sub-issue is closed]
PlanReview --> Accepting : request the acceptance check\n[every sub-issue is closed]
PlanReview --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\na Maintainer adds ready to a fix sub-issue
Accepting -[#red]-> PlanReview : <color:red>ask for the plan review</color>\n<color:red>[the Planner wrote the acceptance check,</color>\n<color:red>a sub-issue is open, every sub-issue</color>\n<color:red>has exactly one risk label]</color>\n/ cumin notifies
Accepting --> Acceptance : ask for the acceptance\n[the Planner wrote the acceptance check,\n<color:red>every sub-issue is closed</color>]\n/ cumin notifies
Accepting --> Accepting : request the acceptance check again\n[no acceptance check, <color:red>or a sub-issue fails</color>\n<color:red>the split check</color>; first time]
Accepting --> Decision : stop the acceptance check\n[a question, or the same failure\nthe second time]\n/ cumin notifies
Acceptance --> [*] : a Maintainer closes the issue

legend right
  A box is a state: a label on GitHub, without "cumin/status/".
  An arrow is a transition of issue-states.md: [guard] / effect.
  Red: the new transition and the new guards.
endlegend

@enduml
